    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1cb51e13_5b574e04",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-19T17:17:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The \"ABI Compliance\" check fails even with that:\n\n```\ntype \u0027struct fscrypt_operations\u0027 changed\n  member \u0027u64 __kabi_reserved1\u0027 was removed\n  member \u0027union { unsigned int(* get_devices_new)(struct super_block*, struct block_device**); struct { u64 __kabi_reserved1; }; union { }; }\u0027 was added\n```\n\nCan we just update the XML file?\n\nI\u0027m still mystified why the fscrypt structs need to be stable at all.  We do *not* support vendor modules using them.  It makes no sense.",
      "parentUuid": "d4dec0ab_63b9e993",
      "revId": "786c76c6bcad2ed54c8549a59780221c2ec8208e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
