      "author": {
        "id": 1869395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-19T20:24:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ack",
      "parentUuid": "cc268387_4fce27d8",
      "revId": "786c76c6bcad2ed54c8549a59780221c2ec8208e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "18571f33_fbcda2be",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1869395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-19T20:24:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, this is an implementation that could land on the main branch. The \"ABI Compliance\" part would need to be added to the allowed_breaks file to clear the change. I suppose we could also just land it here but this is not a KMI breaking patch.\n\n\u003e I\u0027m still mystified why the fscrypt structs need to be stable at all. We do not support vendor modules using them. It makes no sense.\n\nInteresting, I wonder why it was added to the STG monitoring file then. I\u0027ll have a quick look.",
      "parentUuid": "1cb51e13_5b574e04",
      "revId": "786c76c6bcad2ed54c8549a59780221c2ec8208e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1c30a419_fa12db1c",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1869395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-19T20:38:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Apparently the issue is that `struct super_block` type is exposed to the ABI and one of its members `sb-\u003es_cop` has the `struct fscrypt_operations` type exposed.\n\nIIUC, this change would break users that would set the old `get_devices` right? Is this even a valid usage from a vendor point of view? If not, then it would probably be best to apply the original patch which modifies the signature of the callback here. Instead of taking one of the KABI reserved fields.",
      "parentUuid": "18571f33_fbcda2be",
      "revId": "786c76c6bcad2ed54c8549a59780221c2ec8208e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f5029a79_c9cba1c4",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-19T20:42:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We do not support fscrypt-enabled filesystems as vendor modules, or allow vendor modules to override ext4\u0027s or f2fs\u0027s fscrypt functions.  That would make no sense and be completely unsupportable.  The fact that the struct is visible in the headers doesn\u0027t change that.",
      "parentUuid": "1c30a419_fa12db1c",
      "revId": "786c76c6bcad2ed54c8549a59780221c2ec8208e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "01fb5f26_a34d69c8",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1869395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-19T20:52:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Cool, then I think we could land the original version of the patch that updates the signature of the `op-\u003eget_devices` callback in place and then amend the STG file. This would reduce the diff with upstream and make maintenance potentially easier. Or we could keep the current change as is. Your choice. Either way it LGTM.",
      "parentUuid": "f5029a79_c9cba1c4",
      "revId": "786c76c6bcad2ed54c8549a59780221c2ec8208e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7d9d12a5_c1104a4a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-19T21:14:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Doesn\u0027t work because symbol CRCs change:\n\n```\nERROR: ABI DIFFERENCES HAVE BEEN DETECTED!\nERROR: Report summary:\n\nfunction symbol \u0027int __bh_read(struct buffer_head*, blk_opf_t, bool)\u0027 changed\n  CRC changed from 0x64676d2f to 0xb934f752\n\nfunction symbol \u0027struct buffer_head* __bread_gfp(struct block_device*, sector_t, unsigned int, gfp_t)\u0027 changed\n  CRC changed from 0x21ce0724 to 0x57d2ba49\n\nfunction symbol \u0027void __brelse(struct buffer_head*)\u0027 changed\n  CRC changed from 0x46a2ddac to 0x313d99d0\n  ```\n  \nDefining the field in the old way when `defined(__GENKSYMS__)` doesn\u0027t work either.",
      "parentUuid": "01fb5f26_a34d69c8",
      "revId": "786c76c6bcad2ed54c8549a59780221c2ec8208e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
